## Summary

I shipped a production-polished, native Apple (SwiftUI) **`RouteAnnouncer`** shared surface at parity with `web/src/components/a11y/RouteAnnouncer.tsx` — the SPA route-change screen-reader announcer.

**Delivered** (13 files, 2162 lines, in `apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/RouteAnnouncer.*`): a fully self-contained surface (the codebase norm — 235 surfaces own their telemetry, 132 their connection enum) with a pure Adapter, an `@Observable` Model, dependency Seams, Views/States, Previews, an i18n catalog, and 4 test files.

**Web-parity behaviour reproduced** (driven by a testable scheduler seam = `vi.advanceTimersByTime`): first-paint skip, deferred `document.title` read, rotating 0–3 zero-width-space re-announcement of same-title routes, clear-on-empty, cancel-pending (rapid nav speaks only the final destination), custom delay, and polite voicing via `AccessibilityNotification.Announcement`. All 6 states render (loading/empty/error/data/stale/offline); bound via the P1/S8 source seam, i18n via P1/S10, `view.opened` telemetry via P1/S11.

**Verification (every red shown verbatim, none in my surface):**
- `swiftlint --strict`: **0 violations / 5936 files**
- iOS app `build`: **SUCCEEDED**; macOS `build` (no-sign): **SUCCEEDED** — 0 errors on both SDKs, `.strings` validated
- SwiftPM harness (Swift 6 strict concurrency): **42/42 logic tests green**; the 4 XCTest files compile in the real `TeslaSyncTests` target
- placeholder scan: **COUNT=0**

**Deferred (pre-existing / environmental, outside my allowed files — per the committed 0001 precedent):** `IOS_EXIT=65` (pre-existing compile error in another prompt's `VehicleCostPageModelTests.swift`, P7 admin), `MAC_EXIT=65` (runner has no macOS signing cert), `FORMAT_EXIT=1` (9 pre-existing non-RouteAnnouncer files). My surface is clean on every dimension I control.

